## Dependencies

This project uses the following libraries:

- `Arduino.h` - Core library for Arduino framework.
- `WiFi.h` - Manages Wi-Fi connectivity.
- `WebServer.h` - Provides HTTP server functionalities.
- `WiFiClientSecure.h` - Handles secure client connections.
- `HTTPClient.h` - Manages HTTP client requests.
- `Update.h` - Enables OTA firmware update capabilities.

## Hardware Setup

This section will demonstrate how the different hardware components are assembled and describes the function of each hardware component, facilitating the construction and documentation of a device that visually indicates the stages of provisioning and updating.

### Hardware Components

1. Adafruit ESP32S3 Featherboard
2. Breadboard
3. 1 x Red LED
4. 1 x Yellow LED
5. 1 x Green LED
6. 3 x Resistors (appropriate resistance for the LEDs
7. Wires for facilitating connections
8. 1 x Push button (for OTA updates)

